 "title": "Fifths Lead",
 "category": "80s and synth-pop leads",
 "text": "Sound: a thick, open lead with two notes in each key, a fifth apart, gliding together: the 'power chord' synth line of 80s rock and new wave.\n\nHow it's built: two saws, the second tuned 7 semitones up (a fifth), both following one Slew for the glide; the Ladder filter with an envelope that opens it a little on each note; a Delay. One voice.\n\nPlay: simple melodies (every note is already a fifth), legato slides.\n\nTweak: the second oscillator's TUNE (5 for a fourth, 12 for an octave), the filter envelope's DECAY and the filter's CV, the Slew's times.",
